# Local-dev secrets for `wrangler dev`. Copy to .dev.vars (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# One TENANT_<SLUG> per row of dev/tenants.json, holding a JSON object: the ERP's inbound webhook
# URL as the ERP shows it (Odoo: the Incoming Mail Server's "Webhook URL"; Frappe: the Email
# Account's "Webhook URL" — both embed a per-server key) and the secret shown beside it. The
# default below targets an Odoo dev server on port 8169; Frappe would be
# http://localhost:8000/api/method/cloudflare_email_delivery.api.inbound?key=<key>.
TENANT_DEV='{"inboundUrl":"http://localhost:8169/mail_cloudflare/inbound/dev-server-key","secret":"replace-with-the-secret-the-erp-generated"}'

# Bearer token for the ops API (GET /tenants, …), at least 32 characters. Leave unset and every
# ops route answers 404.
# OPS_TOKEN="dev-ops-token-dev-ops-token-dev-ops-token"

# A Cloudflare Access service token goes inside the tenant's JSON, for when the inbound route sits
# behind an Access policy: "accessClientId" and "accessClientSecret", both or neither.
